The Lukoshko Theorem
The Problem of Contradictions in Foundations

Core Principle:
If we proceed with the Lukoshko (the foundation), we encounter the strawberry (the task). The task inherently contains the foundation, and the strawberry must exist exclusively within the Lukoshko.
The Lukoshko is never empty — there is always +1 already present.

This represents an operator self-similarity of dimension 1, safeguarded against collapse and connectivity disruptions by an infinite manifold.
Rest within dynamics, dynamics within rest.

